+## R36 · Free-text PII redaction gap — Microsoft Presidio as the report-only PII layer → `adapt_cleanroom` → Issue #1784
+
+### The gap (repo evidence, main @ c663369)
+
+`core/contracts/redaction.py` is 647 bytes: a regex over dict **key names**
+(`token|secret|password|api[_-]?key|authorization|private[_-]?key|credential`) that masks the value when a key
+matches. No free-text entity detection, no value-side secret detection, no entity model. Code search on main
+shows it guarding exactly the surfaces where third-party text and internal evidence mix:
+`core/contracts/render_preflight_store.py`, `core/services/render_preflight_service.py` (+ gateway mirror),
+`core/contracts/control_plane.py`, `core/github/scripts/surface_advanced_audit_summary.py`,
+`core/security/intelligence/guardian_ai.py`, `core/runner/agent_runner.py`.
+
+The federation ingests untrusted external text (deep-research/search lanes — supply chain documented in
+#1751/#1755; browser/scrape service) and persists evidence into Redis tiers (#1698 chain) and the 21 `memory_*`
+semantic tools (#1747). PII in those flows reaches LLM prompts, evidence JSON, and durable stores unredacted.
+Under the canonical taxonomy adopted this cycle, that is **OWASP LLM Top 10 2025 → LLM06 Sensitive Information
+Disclosure** — the guard chain mapped in #1733 (R29) currently has no PII control to point at. This lane is the
+concrete LLM06 control; it is the *next row over* from R29, not a re-file of it.
+
