+
+### Migration cost & trade-offs (labeled estimates — nothing executed)
+
+- **Effort: LOW / additive.** Wrap the PII tier behind the existing `core/contracts/redaction.py` entry point;
+  all six call sites keep their import. Key-regex stays as the secret-key tier; Presidio becomes the free-text
+  tier. Pilot = **report-only** (log entity types + counts, no behavior change), enforcement only after a
+  precision review on real federation text.
+- **Trade-offs:** new dependency + model download; CPU inference latency per document; recognizer precision on
+  Bengali/English mixed text is **unknown until a real evaluation runs — no benchmark has been run, none is
+  claimed.**
+- **Security:** self-hosted/offline → no PII egress to third parties (the exact weakness of every rejected
+  SaaS alternative).
+
+### Verdict: `adapt_cleanroom`
+
+Additive docs-first pilot on `core/contracts/redaction.py` (+ its docs), report-only mode, zero infra change,
+then an evidence-gated decision on enforcement. If adopted, register the Presidio tier in the #1733 guard-chain
+LLM06 row.
