+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+
+**why:** SupremeAI's secret redaction SSOT (`core/contracts/redaction.py`, 647 bytes) matches only dict key
+names, so PII in free text — the federation's dominant content type (scraped web text, browser DOM, tenant
+payloads, memory documents) — reaches LLM prompts and durable stores unredacted, exactly the OWASP LLM06 row
+the #1733 mapping (R29) has no control for. Presidio (MIT, 2.2.366, release 2026-10-27, 12k stars, last commit
+today, Python >=3.11) is the mature open-source, self-hosted fix: additive behind the existing entry point,
+zero infra, no egress. The org's own hardening plan already lists Presidio as the PII candidate — this lane
+supplies the verification that plan requires, with zero R-register overlap across R1–R35.
+
+**alternatives_rejected:** AWS Comprehend Detect PII ($0.0001/unit, 3-unit min, 12-month free tier — recurring
+cost + PII egress + lock-in, probed 2026-10-28); Google Sensitive Data Protection ($3.00/GB after 1 GB/mo free
+— same class, probed 2026-10-28); Private AI / Nightfall (proprietary SaaS, same egress/lock-in class, closed
+source); custom spaCy-only NER (re-implements what Presidio ships; spaCy is Presidio's default engine, a
+component not a replacement); gitleaks/trufflehog (secret scanning, wrong problem class). Doing nothing was
+also considered and rejected: the gap sits on the security-evidence surfaces (guardian_ai, agent_runner,
+control_plane) the federation is actively hardening this cycle.
